        <tr> 
          <td valign=top width=500 class="title">Frequently Asked Questions 
            <p></td>
        </tr>
        <tbody> 
        <tr> 
          <td valign=top width=500 class="copy"> 
            <p><span class="headline">When is the album coming out in the USA?<br>
              </span> It's due for release on September 18th on <a href="http://www.spinartrecords.com">SpinArt 
              records</a>. A tour will follow in October, from 6th - 24th.</p>
            <p><br>
              <span class="headline">Why aren't you going to the south of the 
              USA (Texas, Florida, Atlanta etc.)<br>
              </span> We always want to play as much as we can, and going to those 
              places is always great. However, mainly for financial reasons, it 
              was a choice between the top and bottom of the US. It was decided 
              that we do the 'top' as in the south you drive more than you play, 
              paying crew as you do, and that would lose us more money therefore 
              jeopardizing future touring budgeting. So, we are trying to organize 
              something for February. We can only apologise to those fans who 
              are missing out, but believe me, we are sad too.</p>
            <p><br>
              <span class="headline">How do I get the new proposed 'live album'?<br>
              </span> Write to <a href="mailto:bishq@hotmail.com">bishq@hotmail.com</a> 
              for all the details.</p>
            <p></p>
            <p><span class="headline">What's the latest on the 'I love Bis' compilation 
              album?<br>
              </span> We are currently awaiting the go-ahead from Grand Royal/Capitol 
              records who own some of the songs. Once this happens, it will hopefully 
              come out in time for the tour. If not, it will still happen at some 
              point, but only mail order. An ad for the album will be posted as 
              soon as it's ready.</p>
            <p><br>
              <span class="headline">How do I get on your mailing list?<br>
              </span> You can join by entering your email address in the form 
              on the front of our website.</p>
            <p><br>
              <span class="headline">When is the album coming out in Europe?<br>
              </span> At present there is no release date, although it may end 
              up being January as it's taking longer to get the record deal finalized. 
            </p>
            <p><br>
              <span class="headline"> Is it true you're doing something with Chemikal 
              Underground?<br>
              </span> Not the album, but an e.p with 4 tracks for the Chemikal 
              Underground series of e.ps that are limited to 1000 copies. This 
              is released only in the UK. This is scheduled for October.</p>
            <p><br>
              <span class="headline">Why are Bis no longer on Wiiija?<br>
              </span> The main guy who ran and owned Wiiija, Gary Walker left 
              last year. Without his hard work and support it was thought that 
              the album would suffer as a result.</p>
            <p><br>
              <span class="headline">Why are Bis no longer on Grand Royal?<br>
              </span> When it was time to renew the contract Grand Royal split 
              with parent company Capitol Records. During this change to a new 
              major label parent company it was decided that they didn't want 
              to keep Bis. In all honesty this was a good outcome as there had 
              been many problems between Grand Royal and Capitol and the bands 
              were stuck in the middle. </p>
            <p><br>
              <span class="headline">Why are you using a drummer live now?<br>
              </span> This was something that Bis wanted to try out and did so 
              at their London gig with Arab Strap. It was such a success that 
              they want to make it a regular thing. The sound is 10 times as good 
              as it's a drummer IN ADDITION to the original set-up with a sampler 
              and a sequencer.</p>
            <p><br>
              <span class="headline">Who is this drummer?<br>
              </span> He is long term friend Graham Christie, the older brother 
              of Ally, the long term roadie.</p>
            <p><br>
              <span class="headline">Did Manda put out a record on Damaged Goods?</span><br>
              Yes, in a band called 'the Kitchen' with ex-Discount guitarist. 
              The CD had 3 songs, and the 7&quot; had two. Go to <a href="http://www.damagedgoods.co.uk">www.damagedgoods.co.uk</a> 
              for mail order.</p>
            <p><br>
              <span class="headline">Did Manda present a radio show?</span><br>
              Yes, with a co-host called Douglas Anderson for BBC Scotland. The 
              show was called 'Air' and was on Monday nights from 7-9. She did 
              this for 8 months and hopes to do something along those lines again. 
              She stopped doing it when Radio Scotland decided to change it's 
              target audience from 15-25 year olds to 35-55 year olds and thought 
              that an older presenter would be more appropriate.</p>
            <p><br>
              <span class="headline">Why is some of your merchandise so cheap?<br>
              </span> The 'Sale Merch' was a boxful of t-shirts that turned 
              up on our doorstep unexpectedly. In order to make new t-shirts we 
              thought we would sell the old design off cheap.</p>
            <p><br>
              <span class="headline">Why aren't all of your gigs all-ages 
              ones?<br>
              </span> The effort is always made to play to all-ages crowds, and 
              these are generally the best ones. However, mainly in the USA there 
              are very strict laws in cities and it's sadly unavoidable. 
              There are sometimes no venues the appropriate size that are all-ages 
              to play in, and if you just do in-stores you don't get paid.</p>
            <p><br>
              <span class="headline">Is it true that Manda got married?<br>
              </span> Yes, April 21st 2001 in Glasgow. </p>
            <p><br>
              <span class="headline">Are John and Steven married?<br>
              </span>No.</p>

<p><br>
              <span class="headline">What happened to bisnation radio?<br>
              </span>Sadly, we had to withdraw the service.</p>

            <p></p>
